  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Just a few showers and an isolated thunderstorm \nare expected for tonight. \n\nLarge scale uplift is lacking - or even turned negative over the\nregion late this aftn. There are some taller cu in two separate\nlines running NW-SE. We've left PoPs, but not more than 40s, in\nthose areas through 05Z/midnight. But, confidence is low that\nmuch deep convection will develop. With the decided lack of rain\non the regional radar mosaic and only small chances that any \ndevelopment will occur upstream of the flood watch area, we've\ndropped the flood watch. \n\n   -------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Drier, less humid weather returns for Saturday \nand lasts through Labor Day Weekend.\n\nA cold front draped across the PA/NY border will begin its\nsouthward surge tonight, helped by a deepening upper low over \nNew England. This push of northeasterly winds at the surface\nwill usher in cooler and much less humid air for Saturday and\nthe remainder of Labor Day weekend. There could still be a few\nlingering showers in the southwest part of our area into\nSaturday morning, but coverage and intensity of storms will\ntrend considerably lower. With cool temperatures aloft, we can't\nrule out the chance for an isolated shower or two on Saturday\naround the area along with widespread stratocumulus clouds.\nSaturday will still be a few degrees warmer than average for\nthis time of year, but the real relief arrives by Saturday\nnight. Dewpoints and low temperatures will fall into the upper \n40s and 50s areawide by Sunday morning.\n \nOther than some morning valley fog, the weather will be really \nnice for the Sunday and Labor Day Monday. Highs mainly in the \n70s and lows 45-55F both Sunday night and Monday night will be\nideal for outdoor activities. Little if any rain is expected\nalong with abundant sunshine. At this point, it looks like dry\nweather sticks around through at least midweek. After that, the\nridge may build once again along with the associated chance for\na return to the ring of fire.",
